    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0157" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="8" xml:id="d174-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-29T12:12:00+08:00">June 29 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >30?</hi>], 1938—12:12 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:05
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0029. Chinese Foreign Office advises river officially blocked above Lienchiachen
                    from 29 June but off record states river navigable along north bank slow speed
                    another 48 hours. Plan <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> remain Kiukiang
                    unchanged.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d174-f1" n="8" type="source" xml:id="d174-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram from the Commander, United States Yangtze Patrol (Le Breton), to
                    the commanding officer of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy;</hi>
                    transmitted to the Department by the Navy Department.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
